<h3>2.2 User Stories with Gherkin Acceptance Criteria</h3>
<h4>User Story 1: Online Claim Submission</h4>
<blockquote><b>As a</b> vehicle policyholder,</blockquote>
<blockquote><b>I want to</b> submit an insurance claim online with my policy, vehicle, and accident details,</blockquote>
<blockquote><b>So that</b> I do not have to visit a physical insurance branch.</blockquote>
<pre><code>Scenario: Successful claim submission with valid parameters
  Given the policyholder is on the Claim Submission page
  When they enter policy &quot;POL-12345&quot;, vehicle &quot;KA-01-AB-1234&quot;, incident date &quot;2026-10-15&quot;, amount &quot;25000&quot;, and valid description
  And they submit the claim form
  Then the system generates a unique claim number starting with &quot;CLM-&quot;
  And redirects to the confirmation page showing status &quot;SUBMITTED&quot;</code></pre>
<h4>User Story 2: Surveyor Adjudication</h4>
<blockquote><b>As an</b> insurance claim reviewer,</blockquote>
<blockquote><b>I want to</b> view pending claims and update their adjudication status,</blockquote>
<blockquote><b>So that</b> valid claims can be approved promptly.</blockquote>
<pre><code>Scenario: Reviewer approves a pending motor claim
  Given the reviewer is logged into the Reviewer Dashboard
  When they inspect pending claim &quot;CLM-2026-46CC7&quot;
  And change status to &quot;APPROVED&quot; with remark &quot;Vehicle inspection verified&quot;
  Then the claim record updates immediately in the database
  And the tracking view reflects status &quot;APPROVED&quot;</code></pre>
<h3>2.3 Definition of Done (DoD) Checklist</h3>
<p>Before any feature branch can be merged into <code>develop</code> or tagged for release, it must satisfy:</p>
<ul><li>[x] Code strictly compiles against OpenJDK 21 with zero compiler warnings.</li></ul>
<ul><li>[x] Unit test coverage exceeds 80% on service layer logic.</li></ul>
<ul><li>[x] All MockMvc controller endpoints return expected HTTP status codes.</li></ul>
<ul><li>[x] Headless Selenium E2E user journeys execute with 100% pass rate.</li></ul>
<ul><li>[x] Peer code review conducted via Pull Request with documented approval.</li></ul>
<ul><li>[x] Jenkins declarative pipeline builds and validates green.</li></ul>
<pre><code>┘</code></pre>
<hr/>
<h2>Task 3: System Requirements &amp; Architecture Specification</h2>
<h3>3.1 Software Requirements Specification (SRS)</h3>
<h4>Functional Requirements (FR)</h4>
<ul><li><b>FR-01 (Claim Registration)</b>: System must capture policy number, vehicle registration number, driver details, incident date/time, accident location, estimated damage, and incident narrative.</li></ul>
<ul><li><b>FR-02 (Format Validation)</b>: Policy number must match regex pattern <code>^POL-[0-9]{5,10}$</code>; vehicle registration must conform to Indian standard format <code>^[A-Z]{2}-[0-9]{2}-[A-Z]{1,2}-[0-9]{4}$</code>.</li></ul>
<ul><li><b>FR-03 (Unique ID Generation)</b>: System must generate an unforgeable reference ID in the format <code>CLM-&lt;YEAR&gt;-&lt;5-HEX-HASH&gt;</code>.</li></ul>
<ul><li><b>FR-04 (Reviewer Actions)</b>: Authorized reviewers can transition claims between <code>SUBMITTED</code>, <code>UNDER_REVIEW</code>, <code>APPROVED</code>, <code>REJECTED</code>, and <code>SETTLED</code> with mandatory audit remarks.</li></ul>
<ul><li><b>FR-05 (Public Tracking)</b>: Any user with a valid Claim ID can view the current state and milestone timeline without login.</li></ul>
<h4>Non-Functional Requirements (NFR)</h4>
<ul><li><b>NFR-01 (Performance)</b>: Page render time &lt; 1.5 seconds under 100 concurrent requests.</li></ul>
<ul><li><b>NFR-02 (Availability)</b>: 99.9% uptime target backed by automated health checks and rapid recovery.</li></ul>
<ul><li><b>NFR-03 (Security)</b>: Non-root execution within container runtime; form protection against XSS and CSRF.</li></ul>
<ul><li><b>NFR-04 (Observability)</b>: Spring Boot Actuator health and metrics endpoints exposed on <code>/actuator/health</code>.</li></ul>
<h3>3.2 3-Tier Layered Architecture</h3>
<p>The application is structured into three clean logical tiers:</p>
<pre><code>┬────────────────────────────────────────┘
                                  │ HTTP / JSON
 DTO Layer: ClaimSubmissionRequest, ClaimStatusUpdateRequest         │
└─────────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────┘
                                  │ Spring Data JPA / Hibernate ORM
 MySQL 8.0 Engine (Containerized production configuration)           │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘</code></pre>
<h3>3.3 Relational Domain Schema</h3>
<p>The central entity is <code>Claim</code>, modeled in JPA as follows:</p>
<pre><code>@Entity
@Table(name = &quot;claims&quot;)
public class Claim {
    @Id
    @GeneratedValue(strategy = GenerationType.IDENTITY)
    private Long id;

    @Column(nullable = false, unique = true, length = 32)
    private String claimNumber; // e.g. CLM-2026-46CC7

    @Column(nullable = false, length = 30)
    private String policyNumber;

    @Column(nullable = false, length = 20)
    private String vehicleRegistrationNumber;

    @Column(nullable = false)
    private LocalDate incidentDate;

    @Column(nullable = false, length = 120)
    private String incidentLocation;

    @Column(nullable = false, precision = 12, scale = 2)
    private BigDecimal estimatedAmount;

    @Enumerated(EnumType.STRING)
    @Column(nullable = false, length = 20)
    private ClaimStatus status = ClaimStatus.SUBMITTED;

    @Column(length = 500)
    private String reviewerRemarks;

    @Column(nullable = false, updatable = false)
    private LocalDateTime createdAt = LocalDateTime.now();
}</code></pre>
<pre><code>┘</code></pre>
