<h2>Task 5: Feature Development with GitFlow Branching</h2>
<h3>5.1 Branch Creation and Feature Implementation</h3>
<p>Following the GitFlow model, the first core feature branch was spawned from <code>develop</code>:</p>
<pre><code># Switch to develop integration branch
git checkout -b develop

# Create dedicated feature branch for claim submission
git checkout -b feature/claim-submission</code></pre>
<p>On this branch, the following components were built:</p>
<ol><li><b>Domain Layer</b>: [<code>Claim.java</code>](file:///d:/DevOps/src/main/java/com/motorclaim/portal/entity/Claim.java) JPA entity and [<code>ClaimRepository.java</code>](file:///d:/DevOps/src/main/java/com/motorclaim/portal/repository/ClaimRepository.java).</li></ol>
<ol><li><b>DTO &amp; Validation</b>: [<code>ClaimSubmissionRequest.java</code>](file:///d:/DevOps/src/main/java/com/motorclaim/portal/dto/ClaimSubmissionRequest.java) with annotations:</li></ol>
<ul><li><code>@NotBlank(message = &quot;Policy number is required&quot;)</code></li></ul>
<ul><li><code>@Pattern(regexp = &quot;^POL-[0-9]{5,10}$&quot;, message = &quot;Policy must match format POL-XXXXX&quot;)</code></li></ul>
<ul><li><code>@PastOrPresent(message = &quot;Incident date cannot be in the future&quot;)</code></li></ul>
<ul><li><code>@DecimalMin(value = &quot;100.00&quot;, message = &quot;Estimated damage must be at least 100&quot;)</code></li></ul>
<ol><li><b>Service Layer</b>: [<code>ClaimServiceImpl.java</code>](file:///d:/DevOps/src/main/java/com/motorclaim/portal/service/impl/ClaimServiceImpl.java).</li></ol>
<ol><li><b>UI Templates</b>: [<code>submit-claim.html</code>](file:///d:/DevOps/src/main/resources/templates/submit-claim.html) and [<code>claim-success.html</code>](file:///d:/DevOps/src/main/resources/templates/claim-success.html).</li></ol>
<h3>5.2 Pull Request Workflow (PR #1)</h3>
<p>The feature was merged via a formal Pull Request:</p>
<pre><code># Stage feature changes
git add src/

# Commit using conventional format
git commit -m &quot;feat(claim): implement core motor insurance claim submission workflow and validation&quot;

# Switch to develop and execute non-fast-forward merge
git checkout develop
git merge --no-ff feature/claim-submission -m &quot;merge: PR #1 - Implement core motor insurance claim submission workflow&quot;</code></pre>
<pre><code>┘</code></pre>
<hr/>
<h2>Task 6: MVP Completion, Collaboration &amp; Merge Conflict Resolution</h2>
<h3>6.1 MVP Capability Completion</h3>
<p>In Task 6, the reviewer adjudication dashboard ([<code>reviewer-dashboard.html</code>](file:///d:/DevOps/src/main/resources/templates/reviewer-dashboard.html)) and self-service tracking view ([<code>track-claim.html</code>](file:///d:/DevOps/src/main/resources/templates/track-claim.html)) were completed, finalizing the Minimal Viable Product.</p>
<h3>6.2 Merge Conflict Simulation &amp; Manual Resolution</h3>
<p>To demonstrate real-world collaborative version control, a concurrent conflict was induced between <code>develop</code> and <code>feature/reviewer-approval-flow</code> on <code>src/main/resources/application.properties</code>:</p>
<ol><li><b>Change on <code>feature/reviewer-approval-flow</code></b>:</li></ol>
<pre><code>   app.features.reviewer-workbench.enabled=true</code></pre>
<p>Committed as <code>feat(review): enable reviewer workbench feature toggle</code>.</p>
<ol><li><b>Divergent change on <code>develop</code></b>:</li></ol>
<pre><code>   app.features.reviewer-workbench.enabled=false-maintenance-mode</code></pre>
<p>Committed as <code>chore(config): set reviewer feature toggle to maintenance mode on develop</code>.</p>
<ol><li><b>Triggering the Conflict</b>:</li></ol>
<pre><code>   git checkout develop
   git merge feature/reviewer-approval-flow</code></pre>
<p>*Git Output*:</p>
<pre><code>   Auto-merging src/main/resources/application.properties
   CONFLICT (content): Merge conflict in src/main/resources/application.properties
   Automatic merge failed; fix conflicts and then commit the result.</code></pre>
<ol><li><b>Resolution</b>:</li></ol>
<p>The conflict markers (<code>&lt;&lt;&lt;&lt;&lt;&lt;&lt; HEAD</code>, <code>=======</code>, <code>&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;</code>) were inspected. The team decided that active feature enablement was required for the MVP:</p>
<pre><code>   # Conflicted block resolved to:
   app.features.reviewer-workbench.enabled=true</code></pre>
<p>The resolved file was staged and committed:</p>
<pre><code>   git add src/main/resources/application.properties
   git commit -m &quot;fix(merge): resolve reviewer feature toggle conflict between develop and feature branch&quot;</code></pre>
<h3>6.3 Semantic Version Tagging</h3>
<p>Two formal immutable release points were tagged:</p>
<pre><code>git tag -a v1.0.0-mvp -m &quot;Release v1.0.0-mvp: Verified working Minimal Viable Product&quot;
git tag -a v1.1.0-complete -m &quot;Release v1.1.0-complete: Full feature release with reviewer approval flow&quot;</code></pre>
<pre><code>┘</code></pre>
