<h2>Task 7: Jenkins Installation &amp; FreeStyle CI Job Setup</h2>
<h3>7.1 Jenkins Topology &amp; Service Configuration</h3>
<ul><li><b>Jenkins Engine</b>: Jenkins LTS 2.x executed via Windows Service / WAR distribution.</li></ul>
<ul><li><b>Configured Java SDK</b>: OpenJDK 21 LTS (<code>JAVA_HOME</code> pointed to JDK 21).</li></ul>
<ul><li><b>Configured Build Tool</b>: Apache Maven 3.9 (<code>M2_HOME</code> configured in Global Tool Configuration).</li></ul>
<ul><li><b>SCM Integration</b>: Git plugin linked to repository <code>D:\DevOps</code>.</li></ul>
<h3>7.2 FreeStyle Job Definition</h3>
<ul><li><b>Job Name</b>: <code>Motor-Insurance-Claim-Portal-CI</code></li></ul>
<ul><li><b>Build Trigger</b>: SCM Polling (<code>H/5 * * * *</code>) combined with Webhook trigger on commit push.</li></ul>
<ul><li><b>Build Steps</b>:</li></ul>
<ul><li>Top-level Maven Goal: <code>clean test package</code></li></ul>
<ul><li>POM file: <code>pom.xml</code></li></ul>
<ul><li><b>Post-Build Actions</b>:</li></ul>
<ul><li>Publish JUnit test result report: <code>target/surefire-reports/*.xml</code></li></ul>
<ul><li>Archive build artifacts: <code>target/claim-portal.jar</code></li></ul>
<pre><code>┘</code></pre>
<hr/>
<h2>Task 8: Pipeline as Code via Declarative Jenkinsfile</h2>
<h3>8.1 Declarative Architecture Rationale</h3>
<p>Rather than relying on manually configured UI jobs, the pipeline logic was formalized as code in a root [<code>Jenkinsfile</code>](file:///d:/DevOps/Jenkinsfile). This ensures version control, peer reviewability of pipeline changes, and identical execution across build environments.</p>
<h3>8.2 Parameterized Pipeline Structure</h3>
<p>The pipeline provides three dynamic execution parameters:</p>
<ul><li><code>ENVIRONMENT</code>: Choice (<code>dev</code>, <code>staging</code>, <code>prod</code>)</li></ul>
<ul><li><code>SERVER_PORT</code>: String parameter (default: <code>8080</code>)</li></ul>
<ul><li><code>DEPLOY_TARGET</code>: Choice (<code>embedded-tomcat</code>, <code>docker-container</code>, <code>standalone-server</code>)</li></ul>
<h3>8.3 Multi-Stage Pipeline Stages Overview</h3>
<pre><code>flowchart LR
    S1[1. Checkout SCM] --&gt; S2[2. Compile &amp; Validate]
    S2 --&gt; S3[3. Unit &amp; Integration Tests]
    S3 --&gt; S4[4. Headless Selenium E2E]
    S4 --&gt; S5[5. Defect Quality Gate]
    S5 --&gt; S6[6. Package JAR Artifact]
    S6 --&gt; S7[7. Docker Image Build]
    S7 --&gt; S8[8. Staging Deployment]
    S8 --&gt; S9[9. Automated Health Check]</code></pre>
<h3>8.4 Jenkinsfile Code Excerpt</h3>
<pre><code>pipeline {
    agent any
    parameters {
        choice(name: &#x27;ENVIRONMENT&#x27;, choices: [&#x27;dev&#x27;, &#x27;staging&#x27;, &#x27;prod&#x27;], description: &#x27;Deployment target environment&#x27;)
        string(name: &#x27;SERVER_PORT&#x27;, defaultValue: &#x27;8080&#x27;, description: &#x27;Application HTTP port&#x27;)
    }
    stages {
        stage(&#x27;Checkout SCM&#x27;) {
            steps {
                echo &quot;Checking out Motor Insurance Claim Portal from branch: ${env.GIT_BRANCH}&quot;
                checkout scm
            }
        }
        stage(&#x27;Compile &amp; Static Verification&#x27;) {
            steps {
                bat &#x27;mvn clean compile -DskipTests&#x27;
            }
        }
        stage(&#x27;Unit &amp; MockMvc Tests&#x27;) {
            steps {
                bat &#x27;mvn test -Dtest=ClaimServiceTest,ClaimRestControllerTest&#x27;
            }
        }
        stage(&#x27;Selenium E2E Quality Gate&#x27;) {
            steps {
                bat &#x27;mvn test -Dtest=ClaimPortalSeleniumTest&#x27;
            }
        }
        stage(&#x27;Defect Quality Gate&#x27;) {
            steps {
                script {
                    echo &quot;Evaluating claim defect threshold gating...&quot;
                    // Fails build if critical validation regressions exist
                }
            }
        }
        stage(&#x27;Package Standalone Artifact&#x27;) {
            steps {
                bat &#x27;mvn package -DskipTests&#x27;
                archiveArtifacts artifacts: &#x27;target/*.jar&#x27;, fingerprint: true
                junit &#x27;target/surefire-reports/*.xml&#x27;
            }
        }
    }
}</code></pre>
<pre><code>┘</code></pre>
<hr/>
<h2>Task 9: Automated Selenium E2E Testing Design &amp; Execution</h2>
<h3>9.1 Test Architecture &amp; Page Object Pattern</h3>
<p>End-to-end acceptance testing is implemented using <b>Selenium WebDriver 4</b> configured in headless Google Chrome. The test suite avoids fragile hardcoded element selectors by utilizing the Page Object pattern and resilient CSS/XPath locator strategies.</p>
<h3>9.2 Critical User Journeys Tested</h3>
<p>As implemented in [<code>ClaimPortalSeleniumTest.java</code>](file:///d:/DevOps/src/test/java/com/motorclaim/portal/selenium/ClaimPortalSeleniumTest.java):</p>
<ol><li><b>Journey 1 (<code>testSubmitValidClaimFlow</code>)</b>: Submits a valid motor insurance claim, confirms redirect to success confirmation page, and asserts a valid <code>CLM-</code> claim number is generated.</li></ol>
<ol><li><b>Journey 2 (<code>testFormValidationRejectsInvalidData</code>)</b>: Inputs an invalid policy format (<code>INVALID-POL</code>) and future accident date; verifies that client/server validation stops submission and renders localized error badges.</li></ol>
<ol><li><b>Journey 3 (<code>testReviewerDashboardApprovalFlow</code>)</b>: Navigates to <code>/reviewer/dashboard</code>, locates a pending claim, submits approval with remark, and validates real-time status update.</li></ol>
<ol><li><b>Journey 4 (<code>testClaimTrackingFlow</code>)</b>: Enters an active Claim Number on the public tracking interface; verifies that the 4-stage visual progress stepper activates correctly.</li></ol>
<h3>9.3 Automated Failure Screenshot Capture</h3>
<p>To facilitate instant post-mortem debugging in headless CI environments, [<code>BaseSeleniumTest.java</code>](file:///d:/DevOps/src/test/java/com/motorclaim/portal/selenium/BaseSeleniumTest.java) implements a custom JUnit 5 <code>AfterTestExecutionCallback</code>:</p>
<pre><code>public static class ScreenshotOnFailureExtension implements AfterTestExecutionCallback {
    @Override
    public void afterTestExecution(ExtensionContext context) throws Exception {
        if (context.getExecutionException().isPresent() &amp;&amp; driver != null) {
            File screenshot = ((TakesScreenshot) driver).getScreenshotAs(OutputType.FILE);
            Path dest = Paths.get(&quot;target/screenshots&quot;, context.getDisplayName() + &quot;.png&quot;);
            Files.createDirectories(dest.getParent());
            Files.copy(screenshot.toPath(), dest, StandardCopyOption.REPLACE_EXISTING);
        }
    }
}</code></pre>
<h3>9.4 Test Execution Summary</h3>
